@Priority W-3 is done, so W-4 is next: it depends on W-3 (done) and is the first ready workflow in the chain. I hold the write lock for the PRD file. W-5 and W-6 wait on their predecessors. Rule: Dependency order first: a workflow runs only after the workflow it depends on is done. One writer at a time on the PRD file, so the lock goes to the first ready workflow in the chain..
HOLD W-5: W-4 (prd-requirements) must be done first
HOLD W-6: W-5 (prd-metrics) must be done first

@Priority W-10 is done, so W-11 (Data flow) is next. It depends on hld-components, which is done, and it is the first ready workflow in the HLD chain. I hold the write lock for the HLD file. W-12 and W-13 wait on their predecessors. Rule: Dependency order first: a workflow runs only after the workflow it depends on is done. One writer at a time on the HLD file, so the lock goes to the first ready workflow in the chain..
HOLD W-12: W-11 (hld-dataflow) must be done first
HOLD W-13: W-12 (hld-hosting) must be done first

@Priority W-17 and W-18 are done. W-19 is next: it depends on lld-interactive (W-18, done) and is the first ready workflow in the LLD chain. I hold the write lock for the LLD file. W-20 and W-21 wait on their predecessors, one at a time. Rule: Dependency order first: a workflow runs only after the workflow it depends on is done. One writer at a time on the LLD file, so the lock goes to the first ready workflow in the chain..
HOLD W-20: W-19 (lld-form) must be done first
HOLD W-21: W-20 (lld-files) must be done first

@Priority W-22, W-23 and W-24 are registered and all rewrite sections of the same LLD file, so I hold the write lock and run them one at a time in registration order. W-22 goes first: its dependency lld-pages is done. W-23 follows once W-22 is done, then W-24. Nothing else is waiting. Rule: Dependency order first, then registration order: a workflow runs only after the workflows it depends on are done. One writer at a time on the LLD file, so the lock goes to the first ready workflow in the list..
HOLD W-23: W-22 must finish first, because only one workflow may write the LLD file at a time
HOLD W-24: W-23 must finish first, because only one workflow may write the LLD file at a time

@Priority W-25, W-26 and W-27 are registered and all rewrite sections of the same LLD file. I hold the write lock and run them one at a time. W-25 (File structure) goes first because its dependency lld-form is done. Please check W-25's envelope: 24 money, 4 calls, 10 minutes, 1 retry. Rule: Dependency order first, then registration order: a workflow runs only after the workflows it depends on are done. One writer at a time on the LLD file, so the lock goes to the first ready workflow in the list, here W-25..
HOLD W-26: W-25 must finish first, because only one workflow may write the LLD file at a time
HOLD W-27: W-25 (which rewrites lld-files) and W-26 must finish first, because only one workflow may write the LLD file at a time
